--- !u!114 &880000001
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 57351767}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8d5f02a3c9e5f7b0a2d4e6f8b9c0d1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  speakerName: NPC Bass
  dialoguePages:
  - "Hmph. Kit. You're strong\u2026 for a local. I'm still the strongest around\u2014don't
    forget it."
  - I'm only here because Dr. Wily sniffed out powerful energy crystals in this dimension.
    Not charity.
  - Found some scrap of paper stuck under my charge cell crate. Said if you hold
    attack to charge, you can move again once your aura shows. Hmph. Cute. Mine's
    still better.
  dialoguePagesMalice:
  - Malice. Joke of a 'boss.' Your little robot parade doesn't impress me.
  - "I'm the strongest around. Wily wants the crystals here\u2014I'm collecting.
    You're just scenery."
  - Some crumpled paper blew against my boot while I was polishing the buster. Whatever.
    Scram.
  dialoguePagesCount:
  - "Count. Finally\u2014someone worth sparring. Hyper Speed and clock-hand shots\u2026
    respectable."
  - Don't get cocky. I'm still the strongest around. Wily sent me for the crystals,
    not a friendship bracelet.
  - "Paper wedged in my ammo belt this morning. Said Up-Hyper slows you too\u2014dashes
    and shots crawl\u2014while Down-Hyper keeps you sharp in a slow world. Efficient.
    Still weaker than me."
  dialoguePagesHarlie:
  - "Harlie\u2026 I don't get you. Sword out, weird calm, zero sense. What are you
    even thinking?"
  - "Whatever. I'm the strongest around. Dr. Wily wants energy crystals from this
    dimension\u2014I'm not here for riddles."
  - "Something on paper fluttered out of my lunch tin\u2014pogo bounce, charge-kick
    windows\u2026 Fine. Swing smarter than you stare."
  interactRadius: {fileID: 0}
  interactCollider: {fileID: 0}
  interactableSymbolBox: {fileID: 0}
  interactSymbolPrefab: {fileID: 4100001001001001004, guid: e1a8c35d6f2b8c0e3d5a7b9c1e2f3a4b, type: 3}
  interactSymbolInstance: {fileID: 0}
  stickUpThreshold: 0.5
  shopAfterDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  spriteRenderer: {fileID: 0}
  spriteFacesLeft: 1
  groundCheck: {fileID: 0}
  groundCheckRadius: 0.15
  groundLayers:
    serializedVersion: 2
    m_Bits: 0
--- !u!114 &880000002
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 372441557}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8d5f02a3c9e5f7b0a2d4e6f8b9c0d1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  speakerName: Kit's mom
  dialoguePages:
  - "Kit, love\u2014Malice has her robots rattling the fences again. Be careful out
    there."
  - Eat before you charge out. Heroes still need dinner.
  - "Oh\u2014while I was folding laundry I found a scrap of paper in your sock drawer.
    It said on the ground your feet lock when you shoot, until that charge aura shows\u2026
    then you can run while charging. Weird place for advice, but it sounded useful."
  dialoguePagesMalice:
  - Malice. Get off my doorstep. Army boss or not, you're not welcome here.
  - Those machines already scare the kids. Don't make this street your battlefield.
  - I was sweeping the porch and a paper slipped out from under the mat. Didn't like
    what it implied about you. Leave.
  dialoguePagesCount:
  - "Count\u2014thank you for watching over Kit. That Hyper Speed of yours buys this
    whole street breathing room."
  - Come in if you need water. When you stretch a second, even tired heroes remember
    to drink.
  - "While I was hanging wash, a paper caught on the line. Hold Up or Down with Dash
    to toggle Hyper Speed\u2014save some of the sixteen seconds so you don't hit
    that weak cooldown. Clever\u2026 and oddly specific."
  dialoguePagesHarlie:
  - Harlie! Careful with that sword near the teacups.
  - Malice's bots have been bold lately. Cut carefully, dear.
  - "I found paper tucked in the sugar jar\u2014don't ask how. It said keep your
    combo going and bounce down on their heads. Textbook sword work, if a little
    sticky with sugar."
  interactRadius: {fileID: 0}
  interactCollider: {fileID: 0}
  interactableSymbolBox: {fileID: 0}
  interactSymbolPrefab: {fileID: 4100001001001001004, guid: e1a8c35d6f2b8c0e3d5a7b9c1e2f3a4b, type: 3}
  interactSymbolInstance: {fileID: 0}
  stickUpThreshold: 0.5
  shopAfterDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  spriteRenderer: {fileID: 0}
  spriteFacesLeft: 1
  groundCheck: {fileID: 0}
  groundCheckRadius: 0.15
  groundLayers:
    serializedVersion: 2
    m_Bits: 0
--- !u!114 &880000003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1758978140}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8d5f02a3c9e5f7b0a2d4e6f8b9c0d1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  speakerName: Kit's dad
  dialoguePages:
  - "Kit\u2014Malice pushed another robot wave through the outskirts. I'll patch
    the fence; you handle the scrap."
  - Proud of you. Still wish you'd sleep more.
  - "While I was stacking lumber, a scrap of paper fell out between the boards. Said
    dash, then jump\u2014you keep that dash-jump speed until you land. Don't waste
    the momentum."
  dialoguePagesMalice:
  - Malice. Army boss or not, you're not stomping this yard.
  - Keep those bots off my lumber pile.
  - "Paper fluttered out of my toolbox while I was tightening a hinge. Whatever it
    said about grapples\u2014practice elsewhere."
  dialoguePagesCount:
  - Count. Heard you slowed the whole street when Malice's bots rolled through. Folks
    still talk about it.
  - If she pushes harder, that Hyper Speed of yours may be what keeps the fences
    standing.
  - "Found paper stuck to a wet paint can. Said Down-Hyper for when you want to stay
    fast while bots crawl\u2014Up-Hyper when you need everything soft, including
    your own dashes and shots. Painter's luck, I guess."
  dialoguePagesHarlie:
  - "Harlie\u2014nice edge on that blade. Malice's bots hate real steel."
  - Don't let them corner you near the sheds.
  - "While shoeing\u2026 well, hammering nails, a paper blew under the workbench.
    Hold charge past halfway for that sliding kick when you need distance. Sounded
    like it knew your sword."
  interactRadius: {fileID: 0}
  interactCollider: {fileID: 0}
  interactableSymbolBox: {fileID: 0}
  interactSymbolPrefab: {fileID: 4100001001001001004, guid: e1a8c35d6f2b8c0e3d5a7b9c1e2f3a4b, type: 3}
  interactSymbolInstance: {fileID: 0}
  stickUpThreshold: 0.5
  shopAfterDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  spriteRenderer: {fileID: 0}
  spriteFacesLeft: 1
  groundCheck: {fileID: 0}
  groundCheckRadius: 0.15
  groundLayers:
    serializedVersion: 2
    m_Bits: 0
--- !u!114 &880000004
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1953892409}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8d5f02a3c9e5f7b0a2d4e6f8b9c0d1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  speakerName: Scratch
  dialoguePages:
  - "Kit! Did you see your rocket at the end of town? I added a new booster fin this
    morning. Well, half a fin. The other half is still a sketch."
  - "When it's flight-ready, the first test is a race: you in the rocket, me on my
    jet board. If I lose to my own invention, I'm blaming your piloting."
  - "Until then, I need you testing gear for me. Tap down plus jump on a thin platform
    and your boots will drop you right through it. Handy when a bot is waiting up top."
  - "Bring me crystals and I'll upgrade that gear in my shop. Quicker charge, stronger
    shots, longer hovers. The rocket can wait while I tune you up."
  dialoguePagesMalice:
  - "Malice. Your bots knocked over my signal tower again. Boss of the robot army,
    and still the worst neighbor on the block."
  - "Claws down. The town kids are watching, and I don't need them picking up tricks
    from you."
  - "I'll admit one thing about those claws: a clean slash can knock shots right out
    of the air. Maybe aim that at your own army for once."
  - "...Fine. My shop doesn't turn anyone away, and crystals are crystals. Bring some
    and I'll upgrade your gear. Doesn't mean I like you."
  dialoguePagesCount:
  - "Count! Every time you use Hyper Speed, the whole town gets a breather. Even my
    scanners go quiet."
  - "Seriously, thank you. Those quiet seconds let me work on Kit's rocket without
    a bot rattling the hull."
  - "I've been studying your Hyper Speed readings. You can still dash while it's active,
    and the same Up/Down+Dash hold cancels it."
  - "Bring me crystals and I'll build on that in my shop. Extra air jumps, full-power
    shots back to back. Whatever helps you keep buying us those seconds."
  dialoguePagesHarlie:
  - "Harlie! That sword sing is still my favorite sound in town. I even set my workshop
    alarm to match it."
  - "Keep cutting through Malice's bots. Every one you stop is one less wandering near
    Kit's rocket."
  - "Here's a trick for your boots: bounce off enemies with that pogo strike, then
    chain right into your combo. It keeps you up high and swinging."
  - "Bring me crystals and I'll upgrade your gear in my shop. Extra air jumps, a charge
    kick that's ready in no time. Come take a look."
  interactRadius: {fileID: 0}
  interactCollider: {fileID: 0}
  interactableSymbolBox: {fileID: 0}
  interactSymbolPrefab: {fileID: 4100001001001001004, guid: e1a8c35d6f2b8c0e3d5a7b9c1e2f3a4b, type: 3}
