--- !u!114 &880000009
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 602281050}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8d5f02a3c9e5f7b0a2d4e6f8b9c0d1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  speakerName: Old Man Cat
  dialoguePages:
  - "Kit, child\u2014Malice has bothered this valley longer than your boots are old."
  - You keep the robots out; we keep the lanterns lit.
  - While trimming the lantern wicks I found paper tucked in the oil tin. Charge
    until the aura shows if you need to move while powering up. Patience, then motion.
  dialoguePagesMalice:
  - "Malice. I've seen worse days\u2026 and better manners from army bosses."
  - Spare my shutters.
  - "A scrap of paper blew under my rocking chair. Slash, grapple, dash\u2014three
    answers. Use them on robots, not porches."
  dialoguePagesCount:
  - Count. Time bends for you, and this valley is gentler for it.
  - "You make minutes matter around here\u2014lanterns stay lit a little longer."
  - Paper was pressed inside my old almanac. Down-Hyper to stay quick while the street
    crawls; Up-Hyper when you want soft falls and careful, slow shots. Rushing wastes
    the gift.
  dialoguePagesHarlie:
  - "Harlie\u2014your sword remembers older wars than this valley. Steady."
  - Steel doesn't negotiate with Malice's army.
  - "Found paper in the bird feeder, somehow. Pogo bounce keeps you above their grabs\u2014stay
    airborne when the pack closes in."
  interactRadius: {fileID: 0}
  interactCollider: {fileID: 0}
  interactableSymbolBox: {fileID: 0}
  interactSymbolPrefab: {fileID: 4100001001001001004, guid: e1a8c35d6f2b8c0e3d5a7b9c1e2f3a4b, type: 3}
  interactSymbolInstance: {fileID: 0}
  stickUpThreshold: 0.5
  shopAfterDialogue: {fileID: 0}
